# Runtime image build context. The Dockerfile COPYs only `app/` (production); the test
# stage mounts the source at run instead of baking it. Exclude everything that must never
# enter an image or would bust the build cache.

# Git
.git
.gitignore

# Python / caches — at EVERY depth: a bare pattern matches only at the context root, so
# `__pycache__` alone left app/**/__pycache__ in the image.
**/__pycache__
**/*.py[cod]
*.so
.Python
.venv
venv/
env/
ENV/
.mypy_cache/
.ruff_cache/
.pytest_cache/
.coverage
htmlcov/

# Secrets / env — must NEVER enter the image, at ANY depth: a bare `.env.*` matches only at the
# context root, so a gitignored app/.env.local shipped inside app/ (only .env.example is harmless)
**/.env
**/.env.*
!.env.example
# Editor backups beside source (app/config.py~ would ship a stale copy of the code)
**/*~

# Runtime output + quarantined legacy files (bind-mounted / local-only, never baked)
**/output/
**/export/
src/

# Docs / dashboards (not needed in the runtime image)
docs/
grafana/
*.md

# Compose / Dockerfiles / build tooling
compose*.yaml
compose*.yml
Dockerfile*
Makefile

# OS / editor
**/.DS_Store
**/Thumbs.db
*.swp
.vscode/
.idea/

# Claude
.claude/
